      "id": 90529,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-02-10T19:47:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Shooting at the main engine of a flying fortress - BAD.&nbsp; Using Blinding Speed to safely remove it from the premises - GOOD.&nbsp; (Flash Flood doesn't quite make sense, and Bio-Engineering Beam makes no sense at all, but still, the idea that you don't want to ATTACK a giant nuclear-or-whatever reactor is pretty grokkable.)</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Really? You can flex some abstract thought muscles here if you wanted to.</p>\n<p>Maybe Tempest washed all the batallion members away from the Engine, securing it's safety (for the moment). Bio-Engineering Beam could be Omni-X interfacing with the tech to make it safe and stable.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>There is a narrative to be made if you want it to.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:15:53.874Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
